# WS6-02 (std.iff boundary cases). Sources: spec/appendix-stdlib.md §24 (ilbmInfo: `ok`
# requires BMHD and one non-empty BODY, width/height 1..1024, depth 1..8, masking 0,
# compression 0/1, wrapped FORM or chunk sizes rejected; ilbmDecode clears and writes
# width*height pixels, "never traps on bad input", false on truncated body or bad RLE;
# ilbmPalette copies whole triplets, missing CMAP returns 0; ilbmPixelHash is FNV-1a)
# and the IFF-85/ILBM format (odd chunks are padded; ByteRun1 control -128 is a no-op).
# Cases (generated by the assessment session; data inline): A a valid 8x2x1 image with a
# 2-colour CMAP; B a BODY size of 0xFFFFFF00; C a FORM length beyond the data; D a BODY
# one byte short; E a ByteRun1 literal run longer than the row; F a ByteRun1 repeat run
# longer than the row; G a 5-byte (odd, padded) CMAP; H depth 9; I a ByteRun1 -128 no-op
# before valid runs; J empty data. Hash values are FNV-1a over the 64-byte pixel buffer
# (computed from the definition: offset 2166136261, prime 16777619).
# Expected: the lines below on every profile and build line, no fault, no sanitizer
# report.
profiles: host hosted-amiga hosted-amiga-13
expect: output
contrast: report("A-valid", a); ==> report("A-valid", c);
contrast-expect: output
--- output
A-valid true true 2 2124478297
B-huge-body false false 0 3755895493
C-form-too-long false false 0 3755895493
D-truncated false false 0 3755895493
E-rle-literal-overrun true false 0 3755895493
F-rle-repeat-overrun true false 0 3755895493
G-odd-cmap true true 1 2124478297
H-depth-9 false false 0 3755895493
I-rle-noop true true 0 2124478297
J-empty false false 0 3755895493
--- contrast-output
A-valid false false 0 3755895493
B-huge-body false false 0 3755895493
